window.docContents[195].resolve({"/Haikus-about-cats/SUTD-Cats/#The-Den--Haikus-about-cats--SUTD-Cats":{"contents":"\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n","context":"The Den\u0009Haikus about cats","header":"1.3. SUTD Cats","id":"/Haikus-about-cats/SUTD-Cats/#The-Den--Haikus-about-cats--SUTD-Cats"},"/Useless-Ramblings/A-mental-note-on-prescriptive-versus-descriptive/#The-Den--Useless-Ramblings--A-mental-note-on-prescriptive-versus-descriptive":{"contents":"Many discussions and debates I have with my friends go in circles and get messily tangled because of implicit mixing-up between descriptive and prescriptive statements; people (including me) tend to use both modes, and switch back and forth between them without making it clear.\n\nI think it would be nice to have some general framing to reach for when this occurs -- I think the key is just to treat \"descriptive\" as the larger framing than \"prescriptive\".\n\nWhen a person is being prescriptive, they are expressing what they think a system should be transformed into. This implies the existence of a larger system that includes that person + the smaller system they're being prescriptive about. Expressing that larger system would be being descriptive about the same issue.\n\n","context":"The Den\u0009Useless Ramblings","header":"3.2. A mental note on prescriptive versus descriptive","id":"/Useless-Ramblings/A-mental-note-on-prescriptive-versus-descriptive/#The-Den--Useless-Ramblings--A-mental-note-on-prescriptive-versus-descriptive"}});